 # NDC Ray Transformation
 
-Also called: NDC Ray Conversion, NDC Ray Conversion for Forward-Facing Scenes, NDC rays, Non-Deterministic Coordinates (NDC) Ray Transformation, Normalized Device Coordinates Ray Transform
+Also called: NDC Ray Conversion, NDC Ray Conversion for Forward-Facing Scenes, NDC Rays, Non-Deterministic Coordinates (NDC) Ray Transformation, Non-Dominated Coordinates (NDC) Ray Transformation, Normalized Device Coordinates Ray Transform, Unbounded Scene Ray Transformation
 
 ## Overview
-The NDC Ray Transformation maps camera-space rays into a normalized device coordinate (NDC) cube $[-1, 1]^3$ to enable uniform sampling in disparity (inverse depth) for forward-facing scenes with unbounded depth [S1][S2, S4, S8, unofficial]. Unlike standard ray generation which samples metric depth linearly, this method shifts ray origins to the near plane and projects them such that linear sampling in the transformed NDC parameter $t'$ corresponds to linear sampling in disparity from the near plane to infinity [S1][S4, unofficial]. This allows rendering scenes extending to infinity within a fixed bounding volume, a requirement for real-world forward-facing captures like those in the LLFF dataset [S1][S4, unofficial].
